            <ArticleTitle>[Treatment of recurrent stenosis by conventional re-PTCA].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>99-101</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Balloon angioplasty for restenosis has a higher success rate and a lower complication rate as compared to PTCA in de-novo-lesions. The restenosis rate after a second or third PTCA is only slightly higher than after a first PTCA. So far, balloon dilatation is the most effective and most economic treatment for restenosis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
